Subject: [PATCH] arm64: point WebKit's ICU at the full break-iterator data

arm64 has no HaikuPorts-built icu74 yet (see 0014's note on openssl3), so
every package here -- bootstrap or not -- uses the bootstrap-profile icu74
package. Its lib/libicudata.so.74 turns out to be a stub: ~130 KiB, versus
the ~30 MiB data/icu/74.1/icudt74l.dat shipped right alongside it in the
same package and never loaded by anything by default. The stub still
exports the icudt74_dat symbol, so most ICU use (collation, number
formatting) works -- but WebKit's break iterators need real locale and
break-rule resources from that data, and WTF::TextBreakIteratorICU's
constructor crashes the process when ubrk_open() fails even with an empty
("root") locale, which the stub can't satisfy:

    WTF::TextBreakIteratorICU::TextBreakIteratorICU(WTF::StringView, ...)
    RELEASE_ASSERT(m_iterator); / RELEASE_ASSERT(U_SUCCESS(status));

debug_server then kills the whole team. In practice this fires on any page
whose layout needs real text measurement -- opening google.com in
WebPositive reproduces it every time (flexbox + ComplexTextController +
ubrk_open for UBRK_LINE), confirmed via the debugger stack trace in the
serial log.

ICU_DATA is ICU's own documented override: point it at a directory holding
icudt<ver><endian>.dat and ICU reads from there for anything the loaded
common library can't supply. The real data is already on disk -- this just
tells ICU to use it. data/system/boot/SetupEnvironment is `env`-sourced by
the `desktop` target in data/launch/user, so everything launched from
Deskbar/Tracker (WebPositive included) inherits it; gated on `uname -m`
so it's a no-op on any architecture that isn't missing a real icu74.

--- a/data/system/boot/SetupEnvironment
+++ b/data/system/boot/SetupEnvironment
@@ -26,6 +26,20 @@
 export BEINCLUDES
 export BE_HOST_CPU
 
+if [ "`uname -m`" = "arm64" ] && [ -f /boot/system/data/icu/74.1/icudt74l.dat ]; then
+	# arm64 has no HaikuPorts-built icu74 yet, so the image ships the
+	# bootstrap-profile icu74 package instead. Its libicudata.so.74 is a
+	# near-empty stub (~130 KiB) -- missing locale and break-iterator data
+	# that WebKit relies on (ubrk_open() for text layout) -- while the full
+	# ~30 MiB dataset ships right alongside it as a loose .dat file nothing
+	# loads by default. ICU_DATA tells ICU to read from that file instead.
+	# Without it, WebPositive calls RELEASE_ASSERT(U_SUCCESS(status)) in
+	# WTF::TextBreakIteratorICU and the process is killed by debug_server
+	# on any page complex enough to need a real break iterator (e.g. a
+	# flexbox layout with text -- google.com, reliably).
+	export ICU_DATA=/boot/system/data/icu/74.1
+fi
+
 if [ "$SAFEMODE" != "yes" ]; then
 	export PATH=.:$HOME/config/non-packaged/bin:$HOME/config/bin:$HOME/config/apps:/boot/system/non-packaged/bin:/bin:/boot/system/apps:/boot/system/preferences
 	export LIBRARY_PATH="%A/lib:$HOME/config/non-packaged/lib:$HOME/config/lib:/boot/system/non-packaged/lib:/boot/system/lib"
